<title>FINLAND: TAMRO JAN-JUNE SALES FELL TWO PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>TAMRO JAN-JUNE SALES FELL TWO PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tamro group said in a</p>
<p>statement on Friday its January-June sales fell two percent</p>
<p>year-on-year to 6.14 billion markka.</p>
<p>&quot;Decreased pharmaseuticals sales in Sweden, caused mainly</p>
<p>by a change in the Swedish reimbursement system which led to</p>
<p>hoarding of drugs at the end of the year 1996, resulted in a</p>
<p>fall in sales in the first half of 1997,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>It gave the following sales figures:</p>
<p>			  Jan-June 1997	Yr/yr change</p>
<p>			     (FIM mln)	   (percent)</p>
<p> Tamro total		  6,144		-2.0</p>
<p> Pharma Division	    5,609		-3.0</p>
<p>Medical and</p>
<p> Laboratory Division	  352		+30.0</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
